      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/03/melbourne-cup-2026-poll-record-numbers-turn-their-backs",
      "description": "<p>Growing disdain for gambling and animal cruelty concerns drive sliding interest in race that once ‘stopped the nation’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A record number of Australians are turning their backs on the Melbourne Cup, with more than two-thirds surveyed saying they have low or zero interest in the annual horse race.</p><p>Support for the Melbourne Cup has been sliding consistently for a number of years, but <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/28/guardian-essential-poll-labor-albanese-one-nation-hanson-coalition-ntwnfb\">the Guardian Essential poll</a> found just 9% of Australians said they had high interest in the race now – nearly half the proportion in 2025.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/03/melbourne-cup-2026-poll-record-numbers-turn-their-backs\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
