    },
    {
      "title": "NSW council refuses to show world-renowned Gaza artwork over ‘unacceptable’ safety risk",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/03/shoalhaven-council-refuses-to-show-wall-of-tears-gaza-artwork-safety-risk-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Shoalhaven council says Wall of Tears installation by Phil Buehler posed risk to staff, visitors and tenants</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A New South Wales local council has refused to show a world-renowned artwork about children killed in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza\">Gaza</a> after asking organisers to investigate hiring “armed guards” to counter the risk of “community conflict” over the mural.</p><p>The organisers, Shoalhaven Friends of Palestine, was aiming to show the Wall of Tears installation by <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2026/jan/30/wall-of-tears-mural-gaza-children-brooklyn\">American artist Phil Buehler</a> at the Shoalhaven Regional Gallery in Nowra on Tuesday, following the work being exhibited around Australia, including on the front lawns of Parliament House in Canberra in September.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/03/shoalhaven-council-refuses-to-show-wall-of-tears-gaza-artwork-safety-risk-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T14:00:44"
    },
