      "description": "<p>Australia’s central bank expected to hit mortgage holders again on Tuesday, as war in Middle East combines with collapsing house prices</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s economy is set for a “sharper, longer slowdown”, major bank economists say, as the Reserve Bank is forced to keep interest rates higher to rid the nation of persistent inflationary pressures.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/minns-warns-rba-rate-rise-job-losses-economy\">The RBA is widely expected to hit mortgage holders with a fifth rate hike</a> on Tuesday, in a move that will push the cash rate to its highest since 2008 amid rising worries the economy could even be tipped into recession.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/australia-economy-fifth-interest-rate-hike-looms\">Continue reading...</a>",
